ey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"ff670fbac62af190e08abaf9ef1910896c53b20b2a5b54b72b5bf20517fb8d37","event_uuid":"a512c197-a19e-4504-b9df-c7fc68ec4794","position":{"commit_sha":"09ff76782659304739a922dceb4d8341feaa3a11","position":"1787452987080858001-a512c197-a19e-4504-b9df-c7fc68ec4794"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"d08786f3cee2f8b3b242ba1d1f1a80f366657609a7821c553b3c9ff59ea6a253","event_uuid":"c55108ed-c6eb-467e-80fa-07a031cde9bb","position":{"commit_sha":"4afb3489cbb2e98707497cb1289697e56d0fdc65","position":"1787455586903390001-c55108ed-c6eb-467e-80fa-07a031cde9bb"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"OPERATOR DECISION (AC1): accepted, via operator-approved task dispatched to this session — implement the provenance marker as proposed. Design adjudication: the marker is an OPTIONAL 'provenance' field on the caused_by LINK event payload with values 'derived' (blame auto-derivation) | 'explicit' (operator/agent-supplied), rather than the sketched 'derived: blame|explicit' spelling — a field named 'derived' holding value 'explicit' is self-contradictory on read. Old events carry no field and read as unknown. No change to the deriver's fail-closed behaviour. Builds on merged change 2125 (77e7-1eec-7b52-46ed, caused_by target validation) — branched from its merge commit d432e3c49b6.","timestamp":1787442972884044001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"EVIDENCE — implemented and merged as Gerrit change 2137 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2137), merged into main as 9fbc28a3588 with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1, 0 unresolved comments. All ACs met: (1) both transition_close write origins populate the marker — tests/unit/test_caused_by_provenance.py asserts 'derived' on the blame path and 'explicit' on the --caused-by path; (2) rebar link … caused_by marks 'explicit' (same file); (3) old unmarked events read as unknown — the replay test shows the dep entry carries no provenance key and reduction succeeds; (4) rebar metrics gains the bug_caused_by_provenance dimension (explicit/derived/unknown counts) in the bug_trends lens, asserted in tests/unit/metrics/test_bug_trends.py; (5) docs/event-schema.md documents the marker and docs/user-guide.md lists the dimension. Additionally the blame-derived backfill (scripts/backfill_caused_by.py) marks its edges 'derived', with a test in tests/scripts/test_backfill_caused_by_heldout.py, and src/rebar/types.py was regenerated from the schemas (Dep gains NotRequired provenance). Review-bot advisory on the reopen-then-reclose-with-explicit-flag no-op keeping the original 'derived' marker: deliberate — bug 10d0 pins that confirming an already-linked target leaves the edge (and its link_uuid/timestamp) untouched; upgrading provenance would rewrite a proven-timestamp edge. Can be revisited as follow-up if escape-rate weighting needs it.","timestamp":1787452955651258001}],"created_at":1787395166332595001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"1d344828-cfc6-4d70-ad2c-0b49728e3de9","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"50e3-6d2a-0e7f-4e92"},{"link_uuid":"ef6cdabc-21e9-409d-9c47-a88cf7e96f3e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"0d4e-439d-5012-4c8b"},{"link_uuid":"e2ff0d8c-1480-4123-ab65-b371675f7103","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"214e-3df3-b70f-4933"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nMeasurement 50e3-6d2a-0e7f-4e92 found the recorded caused_by edges cannot be partitioned into\nblame-derived guesses vs explicitly supplied attributions: `_apply_caused_by`\n(src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py) writes both origins through `_write_link_event` with\nno provenance field, so on read a guessed edge is indistinguishable from a proven one and the\nescaped-defect consumers (`rebar metrics` bug_trends lens, the epic-close caused_by floor)\nweight them identically. The operator accepted this proposal — see the OPERATOR DECISION\ncomment on this ticket — so this ticket now implements the marker. It builds directly on the\nmerged caused_by target validation (change 2125, ticket 77e7-1eec-7b52-46ed).\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd an OPTIONAL `provenance` field to the caused_by LINK event payload, value `\"derived\"`\n(blame auto-derivation) or `\"explicit\"` (operator/agent-supplied). Old events carry no field\nand read as unknown — no migration is needed: the dep schema (`common.schema.json` `$defs/dep`)\nalready allows additional properties, and the reducer surfaces the field present-only (the\nsame pattern as the comment `source_*` provenance fields).\n\n- `rebar.graph._links._write_link_event` gains an optional `provenance` parameter, included in\n  the LINK event data only when set.\n- `transition_close._apply_caused_by` passes `\"explicit\"` when the close carried a non-empty\n  `--caused-by`, `\"derived\"` when the culprit came from `blame.derive_caused_by`. No change to\n  the deriver's fail-closed behaviour (the strict-majority abstention stays as designed).\n- `add_dependency` (the `rebar link` path shared by CLI/library/MCP) marks caused_by writes\n  `\"explicit\"` — a linked attribution is supplied by the caller, never blame-derived. Other\n  relations are unchanged (no field written).\n- `reducer/_processors.py process_link` copies `provenance` onto the dep entry present-only,\n  so replay of old unmarked events yields the exact prior dep shape.\n- `common.schema.json` documents the optional enum on the dep def.\n- `rebar metrics`: bug_trends rows carry per-edge provenance and a new STOCK dimension\n  `bug_caused_by_provenance` reports the explicit/derived/unknown edge counts, so escape-rate\n  consumers can weight proven attributions above guessed ones. `bug_caused_by_fan_in` keeps\n  its existing shape.\n\n## Scope\n\n- src/rebar/graph/_links.py — `_write_link_event` provenance param; `add_dependency` marks\n  caused_by explicit.\n- src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py — `_apply_caused_by` selects derived vs explicit.\n- src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py — `process_link` surfaces the field present-only.\n- src/rebar/schemas/common.schema.json — optional `provenance` property on the dep def.\n- src/rebar/metrics/bug_trends.py — per-edge provenance in rows + the\n  `bug_caused_by_provenance` dimension.\n- docs/event-schema.md, docs/user-guide.md — document the marker and the new dimension.\n- tests/unit/test_caused_by_provenance.py (new) — write-site and replay coverage.\n- tests/unit/metrics/test_bug_trends.py — the new dimension's derivation.\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit tests, written RED-first: (1) a bug close with an EMPTY `--caused-by` and a stubbed blame\nculprit writes the edge with provenance `\"derived\"`; (2) a close with an explicit `--caused-by`\nwrites `\"explicit\"`; (3) `rebar link <bug> <origin> caused_by` writes `\"explicit\"`;\n(4) legacy/failure path — replay of a pre-marker LINK event (no field) reduces to a dep entry\nWITHOUT a provenance key (shape unchanged, reduction succeeds), and blame returning no culprit\nstill writes nothing; (5) `bug_caused_by_provenance` counts explicit/derived/unknown edges and\nreturns None when no caused_by edges exist (the unavailable/empty path).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Both transition_close write origins populate the marker: unit tests assert `\"derived\"`\n      on the blame path and `\"explicit\"` on the `--caused-by` path.\n- [x] `rebar link … caused_by` marks `\"explicit\"`: unit test asserts the dep entry's field.\n- [x] Old unmarked events read as unknown: a replay unit test shows the dep entry carries no\n      provenance key and reduction succeeds unchanged.\n- [x] `rebar metrics` distinguishes supplied vs derived edges: the bug_trends lens gains\n      `bug_caused_by_provenance` with explicit/derived/unknown counts, asserted by unit test.\n- [x] docs/event-schema.md documents the marker and docs/user-guide.md lists the new\n      dimension: verified by reading the landed diff.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/graph/_links.py","reason":"_write_link_event optional provenance param; add_dependency marks caused_by explicit"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py","reason":"_apply_caused_by selects derived vs explicit provenance"},{"path":"src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py","reason":"process_link surfaces provenance present-only"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/common.schema.json","reason":"optional provenance enum on the dep def"},{"path":"src/rebar/types.py","reason":"regenerated from the schemas: Dep gains NotRequired provenance (CI staleness gate)"},{"path":"src/rebar/metrics/bug_trends.py","reason":"per-edge provenance in rows + bug_caused_by_provenance dimension"},{"path":"scripts/backfill_caused_by.py","reason":"blame-derived backfill writes must mark derived, or the unknown cohort stops meaning pre-marker"},{"path":"docs/event-schema.md","reason":"document the marker on LINK events"},{"path":"docs/user-guide.md","reason":"list the new bug_trends dimension"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_caused_by_provenance.py","reason":"new write-site and replay coverage"},{"path":"tests/unit/metrics/test_bug_trends.py","reason":"new dimension derivation coverage"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_backfill_caused_by_heldout.py","reason":"backfill provenance=derived assertion (review-bot advisory)"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","0d4e-439d-5012-4c8b"],["relates_to","214e-3df3-b70f-4933"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"63af7467-934b-437f-b4c6-6f2bf3e222d0","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"6536-367c-e358-424d","ticket_type":"task","title":"Proposal: provenance marker (derived vs explicit) on caused_by link events","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["3291d2ca-9e72-4cae-b2e7-695aa414f9e2","9ab41573-2393-442b-b31a-a3668da05b59","0fcb8eea-b33f-403f-aa34-aa467689ab61","9b401fcf-7432-46ff-8aeb-9a987c66803d","63af7467-934b-437f-b4c6-6f2bf3e222d0","fe5b38f5-fb54-48d5-9658-4e8d02f119b6","ef6cdabc-21e9-409d-9c47-a88cf7e96f3e","e2ff0d8c-1480-4123-ab65-b371675f7103","a6df8510-c777-4731-a38e-f381aa88b25d","a512c197-a19e-4504-b9df-c7fc68ec4794","c55108ed-c6eb-467e-80fa-07a031cde9bb"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787461470978106001,"uuid":"93e3eff0-959c-4c33-90d4-6fcdc45a308d"}